WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.462
A subquery in FROM is called a derived table.

00:00:03.462 --> 00:00:06.407
The inner query produces rows and columns.

00:00:06.407 --> 00:00:11.592
The outer query treats those rows like an intermediate table for that statement.

00:00:11.592 --> 00:00:16.207
This is especially useful when you want to aggregate first and then join.

00:00:16.207 --> 00:00:20.327
Always ask what one row in the derived table represents.

00:00:20.327 --> 00:00:24.217
SQL can express the same logic in several forms.

00:00:24.217 --> 00:00:30.387
A good rewrite keeps the same grain and business meaning while changing how work is organized.

00:00:30.387 --> 00:00:36.127
Use EXPLAIN to inspect the plan rather than assuming one style is always faster.

00:00:36.127 --> 00:00:40.160
Performance reasoning should follow correctness, not replace it.
